      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1071069605,
      "text": "Salacca wallichiana is a species of plant in the family Arecaceae. The specific epithet (wallichiana) honors Danish botanist Nathaniel Wallich. It is found in Malaysia, Thailand, Myanmar, and Sumatra. It is valued for its edible fruit which is consumed across its native range."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Salacca wallichiana",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salacca_wallichiana",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 29242245,
      "text": "Salacca wallichiana adalah spesies tumbuhan dalam keluarga Arecaceae. Epitet spesifiknya (wallichiana) menghormati ahli botani Denmark Nathaniel Wallich. Tanaman ini ditemukan di Malaysia, Thailand, Myanmar, dan Sumatra. Tanaman ini dihargai karena buahnya yang dapat dimakan yang dikonsumsi di seluruh wilayah asalnya."
    }
